A||||11||Blaster||Accell coil||||5||
Z||000000||Blaster||07-27-2000||03:31 AM||||This was a problem I had awhile back. I went to a local performance shop and bought an accell coil.  I drove the car for about 2 days and it was fine.  Then on the third day, on my way home, my car lost all power and started back firing.  It died on me.  Waited a couple mins and started it back up.  It would idle alright, but if I touched the gas it would eat it.  Called a friend and he brought me my stock coil.  Threw it in there and it started right up and ran ok again.  I drove it home and threw the accell back in there and it started doing that backfiring crap again.  I went back to the shop I got it from, had to go through a bunch of hassle with them, and they gave me another one.  Drove it to a friends house a installed it.  Drove about two miles and it started the backfiring again and died.  Threw the stock one back in and it ran ok.  Now I went back to the shop and the owner could not figure out what it was. They put a tester on it and said everything looked alright.  Finally I got my money back and just gave up.  <BR>Now the only thing I could think of is that it was retarding my timing. I have 8mm superstock wires on there, and I am sure they could handle it, and I run ACDelco Rapid fires. I thought maybe it was sending bad signals, but to get 2 new coils that both sent bad signals would be a long shot.  No one around here that I know could come up with a reason other than the timing being retarded.  I was thinking about going with the MSD coil, but I don't want to go through the same thing.  Has anyone else had any similar problems like this?  Sorry for the long post. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Blaster||07-27-2000||03:34 AM||||Sorry about the double post, ISP ate it while I was sending the message and I thought it didn't make it.||||reg||8
Z||000002||Gokart||07-27-2000||06:27 AM||||No, just the opposite Blaster. I got 8mm wires too along with the Accel "super" coil and I'm running Bosch platinum+4's. I had probs starting on the first try with the old stock coil and she fires up everytime now with this new set up. I did notice some ill affects at first but I think it was because I hadn't upgraded the wires yet. Maybe I have my timing set slightly different than yours? Good luck.<P>------------------<BR> Marc                     87GT||||reg||5
Z||000003||stimpy||07-27-2000||06:58 AM||||They didn't sell you a universal application coil, did they? It should have looked just like a stock coil except yellow.  I've never had a problem with mine (knocking wood).<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://gifs123.tripod.com/page15/renstimpy2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FieroGTRacingInc||07-27-2000||07:50 AM||||Hey ...  good post guy's...  I have the Accel coil also ,along w/ the 8mm Accel wires too....   just yesterday , i start my 87GT and it was like I had 20% power. My car was just going putt putt putt putt putt putt putt , then all of  a sudden it sounded like it was trying to clear up then it started running fine...   Is my coil going bad too???<BR>                Steve..  85GT,87GT,842m4||||reg||1
Z||000005||Taijiguy||07-27-2000||08:29 AM||||Hey Blaster-<P>You didn't say if you replaced your wirse, cap, and rotor with the coil. The new coil is gonna have a buttload more juice, and may be causing arching wire-to-wire, or wire-to-ground. Or your cap could have a hairline crack that started to carbon up creating a short. I'd check all that, even if you DON'T go back to the Accel, those components could be causing you problems.....<P>-Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000006||ka4nkf||07-27-2000||10:34 AM||||Trust me and get the MSD coil and you will be very pleased, I have heard nothing but good reports on It. I have one and It Is the best improvement I have made on my Fiero.<BR>You will be very happy with It.||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||07-27-2000||03:42 PM||||I use stock plug wires, Bosch Platinum plugs and the Accel Fiero replacemt coil. MY OEM puked so it was only a few more bucks. I have none of the probs youve had and immediatly felt an acceleration improvement.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Blaster||07-27-2000||04:32 PM||||I don't think it is my dist. or cap. because I replaced both of them about a year before I bought the coil and had the problems.  I had the accell 8mm wires on it with the acdelco rapid fires when I was having the problem with the performance.  I think I might try the MSD some time.  It wasn't a universal either, it looked just like my stock one.  Thanks for all the info. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||88formula||07-27-2000||05:08 PM||||I agree with Taijiguy. Your ignition system must have a leak in the circuit somewhere. The stock coil does not produce enough voltage to overcome the resistance of the ignition leak but the Accel coil does. Did you use anti-seize compound on you plugs? It conducts electricity.||||reg||1
Z||000010||contra||07-27-2000||06:49 PM||||i've got the accel supercoil too, looks like the stock one almost but yellow and to be honest i didn't notice any difference. I'm going to try getting thicker sparkplug wires, and maybe a new distributer cap.<BR>i think changing the sparkplugs will only lead to hell so i'm not up for trying to get them out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||theogre||07-28-2000||09:50 PM||||After market coils draw/produce more power than OE. If any part of the system is weak the system may fail when an aftermarket coil is slapped on the car. This applies to all cars.<P>It also affects the PIM. If you have a weak, improperly installed, or hot PIM then odd are good you'll get problems like this. The PIM has to pass more power to the coil. That makes the PIM hotter than it gets with an OE coil. Hot PIM's don't fire well.<P>------------------<BR>Lake Superior? Is that what I stepped in? Sorry.||||reg||1
